  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The initial budget was $500,000, later adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration. The project involves strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI research. Key milestones include a successful prototype test for secure file sharing ahead of schedule, with UI enhancements planned for October. The team expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). A $15,000 training budget was approved for coding teams and project managers. Ideas for AI-enhanced data visualization were solicited by July 20th, with feedback on the prototype requested by the end of November."
